window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-694ea1470b4cc060"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"glossary\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">术语表</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>这份术语表可作为快速参考，帮助你了解 Codex 在桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端、SDK 及相关集成中使用的术语。</p> <p><strong>术语表</strong></p> <blockquote> <p>搜索术语表；按术语、定义或使用界面筛选；没有与搜索内容匹配的术语。</p> </blockquote> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">操作（Action）</a> — 由用户、ChatGPT 或 Codex 执行的一项操作，例如编辑文件、运行命令或使用已连接的服务。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页、移动端、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">智能体（Agent）（需联网）</a> — Codex 智能体会根据上下文进行推理、使用工具并完成任务。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a> — 代码仓库级或用户级的指导文件，用于向 Codex 提供持久有效的指令。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">分析仪表板（Analytics dashboard）</a> — 供管理员查看 ChatGPT 工作区采用情况及 Codex 专项报告的中心页面。</li> <li>适用于: 企业版</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=sign-in-with-an-api-key\">API 密钥登录（API key sign-in）</a> — 使用 OpenAI API 密钥进行身份验证。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=sandbox-and-approvals\">审批策略（Approval policy）</a> — 规定 Codex 在执行操作前必须于何时询问你的规则。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=automatic-approval-reviews\">审批请求（Approval request）</a> — Codex 请求你允许一项受限操作。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">应用（Apps (configuration)）</a> — Codex 配置和应用服务器中用于在 <code>apps</code> 名称下存储连接器设置的字段。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302b8efa03eab38\">应用快照（Appshot）</a> — 发送到 ChatGPT 或 Codex 对话中的最前方应用窗口快照。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=login-caching\">身份验证缓存（Auth cache）</a> — Codex 重复使用的本地已保存登录凭据。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=automatic-approval-reviews\">自动审批审核（Automatic approval review）</a> — 在符合条件的审批请求继续执行之前，由模型对其进行审核。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">定时任务（Scheduled task）</a> — ChatGPT 在未来某一时间或按重复计划运行的提示词；它拥有自己的设置和运行历史记录。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=managing-tasks\">定时运行（Scheduled run）</a> — 定时任务的一次执行，其中包括运行状态以及产生的所有发现。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/browser?surface=app#app-computer-use-in-the-browser\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">浏览器中的 Computer Use（Computer Use in the browser）（需联网）</a> — 让 ChatGPT 能够直接操作内置浏览器的能力。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76?anchor=start-a-chat\">对话（Chat）</a> — 供用户与 ChatGPT 或 Codex 交换消息的已保存空间，包含共享的上下文、结果和操作。Quick chat 可从 Codex 启动 ChatGPT 对话。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页、移动端、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=sign-in-with-chatgpt\">ChatGPT 登录（ChatGPT sign-in）</a> — 使用 ChatGPT 账户和工作区权限进行身份验证。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">计算机历史记录（Computer History）</a> — macOS 上的选择加入功能：它根据获准应用和网站中的交互事件建立记忆和时间线。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex 云端（Codex Cloud）</a> — 在云端运行、拥有各自工作区、代码仓库和工具的编程任务。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、IDE 扩展、网页</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">云端环境（Cloud environment）</a> — 为 Codex Cloud 任务配置、可重复使用的代码仓库、依赖项、工具和访问设置。</li> <li>适用于: 云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=how-codex-cloud-tasks-run\">云端对话（Cloud chat）</a> — 在云端环境中远程运行的 Codex 对话。</li> <li>适用于: 云端</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex（需联网）</a> — OpenAI 面向软件开发任务的编程智能体。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、网页、云端、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT 桌面应用（ChatGPT desktop app）</a> — 同时提供 ChatGPT 和 Codex 的桌面应用，其中包括 Chat、Work、项目、文件预览、定时任务和开发者工具。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex app-server</a> — 本地 JSON-RPC 服务器，用于在自定义客户端中嵌入 Codex 线程、轮次、审批、历史记录和流式事件。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、IDE 扩展、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a> — 用于以交互方式或通过脚本运行 Codex 的终端客户端。</li> <li>适用于: 终端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">codex exec</a> — 通过脚本或持续集成（CI）以非交互方式运行 Codex 的 CLI 命令。</li> <li>适用于: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c7af5bbd57109077\">Codex IDE 扩展（Codex IDE extension）</a> — 让你可以在 VS Code、JetBrains IDE、Cursor 和 Windsurf 等 IDE 中使用 Codex 的编辑器集成。</li> <li>适用于: IDE</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e3c5173f4c4c14ef\">Codex SDK</a> — 用于构建由 Codex 驱动的工作流程或集成的编程接口。</li> <li>适用于: SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=codex-managed-and-permanent-worktrees\">Codex 管理的工作树（Codex-managed worktree）</a> — Codex 为某个对话创建并管理的临时工作树。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=context\">上下文压缩（Compaction）</a> — 总结较早的上下文，使长时间运行的工作能够继续。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">合规 API（Compliance API）</a> — 用于导出受支持的 ChatGPT 工作区记录和审计元数据的 API。</li> <li>适用于: 企业版</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a> — 让 ChatGPT 可以通过用户界面与其它应用交互的桌面能力。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713?anchor=configtoml\">config.toml</a> — Codex 的本地配置文件。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=what-comes-from-the-connected-host\">已连接主机（Connected host）</a> — 为通过远程连接打开的 ChatGPT 或 Codex 对话提供文件、工具和 shell 访问权限的计算机或开发环境。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、移动端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">连接器（Connector）</a> — 插件中的一个组件，用于把 ChatGPT 或 Codex 连接到外部服务中的数据和操作。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用（ChatGPT Work、Codex）、网页（ChatGPT Work）</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76?anchor=start-a-chat\">会话（Conversation）</a> — 在一个对话中，用户与 ChatGPT 或 Codex 持续交换消息和共享上下文的过程。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页、移动端、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=context\">上下文（Context）</a> — Codex 工作时可以使用的信息，例如文件、此前的消息、工具输出和指令。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/api/docs/guides/conversation-state#managing-the-context-window\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">上下文窗口（Context window）（需联网）</a> — 模型一次能够考虑的信息总量上限。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b?anchor=custom-agents\">自定义智能体（Custom agent）</a> — 由用户定义、拥有自己指令和设置的智能体角色。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-4d7a5dc78b3c591e?anchor=deny-reads-with-exact-paths-or-globs\">拒绝读取规则（Deny-read rule）</a> — 阻止 Codex 读取敏感路径或通配符匹配项的文件系统权限规则。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、企业版</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/code-review?surface=app#app-what-changes-it-shows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">差异（Diff）（需联网）</a> — 一组 Git 文件更改，可供检查、评论、暂存或还原。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、Git、审查</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">域名允许列表（Domain allowlist）</a> — Codex Cloud 环境网络策略允许访问的一组域名。</li> <li>适用于: 云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">本地环境（Environment (local)）</a> — 桌面应用中的一项配置，用于告诉 Codex 如何为项目设置工作树。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、工作树</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=environment-variables-and-secrets\">环境变量（Environment variable）</a> — 任务执行期间可用的运行时配置值。</li> <li>适用于: 云端、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a?anchor=basic-usage\">临时会话（Ephemeral session）</a> — 完成后不会保存会话状态的非交互式运行。</li> <li>适用于: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=fast-mode\">快速模式（Fast mode）</a> — 让受支持模型以更高额度成本换取更快响应的速度设置。</li> <li>适用于: CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-4d7a5dc78b3c591e?anchor=filesystem-permissions\">文件系统权限（Filesystem permission）</a> — 授予或拒绝路径读取和写入权限的权限配置规则。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=managing-tasks\">发现（Finding）</a> — 定时任务显示的一项值得注意的结果或问题。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004?anchor=configure-defaults\">完全访问（Full access）</a> — Codex 不受常规沙箱限制地运行的模式。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=whats-a-worktree\">Git 工作树（Git worktree）</a> — 同一个代码仓库的第二份检出，用于并行开展分支工作。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、Git</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=working-between-local-and-worktree\">移交（Handoff）</a> — 在 Local 和 Worktree 之间移动对话及其工作内容。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\">心跳任务（Heartbeat）</a> — 一种重复运行的定时任务，每次都会让 ChatGPT 回到同一个对话。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">钩子（Hook）</a> — 当某个 Codex 事件匹配时运行的生命周期处理程序，例如使用工具、请求权限或某一轮停止时。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4?anchor=config-shape\">钩子事件（Hook event）</a> — 已配置的钩子处理程序可以运行的生命周期节点。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/code-review?surface=app#app-staging-and-reverting-files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">更改块（Hunk）（需联网）</a> — 差异中一段连续的内容，可单独暂存、取消暂存或还原。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、Git、审查</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/code-review?surface=app#app-inline-comments-for-feedback\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">行内评论（Inline comment）（需联网）</a> — 附加到差异中特定代码行上的反馈。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=web-search-mode\">实时网页搜索（Live web search）</a> — 实时查找当前网络信息。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=working-between-local-and-worktree\">本地（Local）</a> — Codex 在用户计算机上工作的模式。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-275a09b4f8630225\">本地对话（Local chat）</a> — 在用户计算机上运行的 ChatGPT 或 Codex 对话。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">托管配置（Managed configuration）</a> — 由组织控制的 Codex 默认值和限制。</li> <li>适用于: 企业版</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> — 模型上下文协议（Model Context Protocol），一种把 Codex 连接到外部工具和上下文的标准。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=supported-mcp-features\">MCP 资源（MCP resource）</a> — MCP 服务器公开的可读上下文，供 Codex 检查。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=supported-mcp-features\">MCP 服务器（MCP server）</a> — 通过 MCP 公开的外部工具或上下文提供方。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=supported-mcp-features\">MCP 工具（MCP tool）</a> — MCP 服务器公开的一项操作，Codex 可以在任务期间调用它。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=macos-managed-preferences-mdm\">MDM</a> — 用于分发设备配置文件和受管理 Codex 设置的移动设备管理工具。</li> <li>适用于: 企业版</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">记忆（Memories）</a> — Codex 可以跨会话重复使用的本地已保存上下文。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">模型（Model）</a> — Codex 用于推理和工具工作的 AI 模型。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=network-access\">网络访问（Network access）</a> — 允许命令或环境访问互联网的权限。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=network-policy\">网络策略（Network policy）</a> — 基于域名的允许和拒绝规则，用于限制沙箱内向外发出的网络流量。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">非交互模式（Non-interactive mode）</a> — 通过脚本或持续集成（CI）运行 Codex 的 CLI 模式。</li> <li>适用于: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a?anchor=create-structured-outputs-with-a-schema\">输出数据结构定义（Output schema）</a> — 传给 <code>codex exec</code>、用于约束最终响应的 JSON Schema。</li> <li>适用于: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=codex-managed-and-permanent-worktrees\">永久工作树（Permanent worktree）</a> — 作为独立项目长期保留的工作树。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-4d7a5dc78b3c591e?anchor=define-and-select-a-profile\">权限配置（Permission profile）</a> — 一项已命名的最小权限策略，把本地命令执行所需的文件系统规则和网络规则组合在一起。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3e83237203418633?anchor=plan-first-for-difficult-tasks\">计划（Plan）</a> — Codex 为完成任务提出或跟踪的步骤。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件（Plugin）</a> — 可安装的能力包，例如技能、连接器和工具；它通过 ChatGPT 与 Codex 共用的通用目录分发。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用（ChatGPT Work、Codex）、网页（ChatGPT Work）、CLI</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件清单（Plugin manifest）</a> — 用于标识插件并指向内含技能、连接器映射、MCP 服务器、钩子和元数据的插件元数据文件。</li> <li>适用于: 插件编写</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6c7aa55b479f9cdd?anchor=understand-the-rules-language\">前缀规则（Prefix rule）</a> — 一种命令规则模式，用于允许匹配的命令前缀、要求执行前请求审批或禁止执行。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、企业版</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=profiles\">配置预设（Profile）</a> — Codex 的已命名配置预设。</li> <li>适用于: CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">渐进式披露（Progressive disclosure）</a> — 只在需要时加载技能细节，以节省上下文。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页（ChatGPT Work）、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">项目（Project）</a> — 一组相关对话和共享来源，或者用于文件工作的本地文件夹。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">提示词（Prompt）</a> — 发送给 ChatGPT 或 Codex 的问题、指令或目标。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/code-review?surface=app#app-pull-request-reviews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">拉取请求审查（Pull request review）（需联网）</a> — Codex 对拉取请求中的更改或反馈进行的审查。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、GitHub</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">RBAC</a> — 针对工作区权限的基于角色的访问控制。</li> <li>适用于: 企业版</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">只读模式（Read-only mode）</a> — Codex 可以检查内容，但未经审批不能进行修改的模式。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=reasoning-effort\">推理强度（Reasoning effort）</a> — 控制模型使用多少推理预算的设置。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f\">远程连接（Remote connection）</a> — 一种连接方式，让你可以通过已连接主机访问另一台设备上的 ChatGPT 或 Codex 对话。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、移动端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713?anchor=requirementstoml\">requirements.toml</a> — 用于受管理 Codex 设置、由管理员强制实施的要求文件。</li> <li>适用于: 企业版</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">审查窗格（Review pane）</a> — 桌面应用中用于检查差异、评论和 Git 更改的视图。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6c7aa55b479f9cdd\">规则（Rules）</a> — 用于允许命令前缀或权限例外、要求执行前请求审批或拒绝执行的策略。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">沙箱（Sandbox）</a> — 用于限制 Codex 命令可以访问或修改哪些内容的强制边界。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=sandbox-level\">沙箱模式（Sandbox mode）</a> — 规定 Codex 文件系统和网络限制的配置。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e3c5173f4c4c14ef?anchor=sandbox-presets\">沙箱预设（Sandbox preset）</a> — SDK 对常用沙箱策略的简写，例如只读、工作区写入或完全访问。</li> <li>适用于: SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">计划时间（Schedule）</a> — 定时任务的时间规则。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=environment-variables-and-secrets\">网络密钥（Network secret）</a> — 特定 HTTPS 服务的凭据。程序会收到一个占位符；对于允许访问的目标，代理会在设置阶段和任务期间代为替换实际凭据。</li> <li>适用于: Codex Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a?anchor=setup-scripts\">设置脚本（Setup script）</a> — 在智能体启动之前运行，用于安装依赖项或准备工具的脚本。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用工作树</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">技能（Skill）</a> — 可重复使用的工作流程包，其中包含指令以及可选的脚本或参考资料。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页（ChatGPT Work）、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23?anchor=how-codex-uses-skills\">技能调用（Skill invocation）</a> — 以显式或隐式方式激活技能。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页（ChatGPT Work）、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">斜杠命令（Slash command）</a> — 以斜杠开头输入，用于控制或检查 Codex CLI 会话的命令。</li> <li>适用于: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">独立定时任务（Standalone scheduled task）</a> — 一种定时任务，每次运行都会启动新对话，并在 Triage 中报告发现。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=stdio-servers\">STDIO MCP 服务器（STDIO MCP server）</a> — 由已配置的命令及参数作为本地进程启动的 MCP 服务器。</li> <li>适用于: CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=streamable-http-servers\">可流式 HTTP MCP 服务器（Streamable HTTP MCP server）</a> — 通过 HTTP 访问的 MCP 服务器，可选择使用 bearer token 或 OAuth 身份验证。</li> <li>适用于: CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">子智能体（Subagent）</a> — 为处理任务的一部分而启动的专用子智能体。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b?anchor=core-terms\">子智能体工作流程（Subagent workflow）</a> — Codex 并行运行受委派智能体并合并其结果的工作流程。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">独立任务（Standalone task）</a> — 未归入某个项目的 Codex 任务。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">任务（Task）</a> — ChatGPT 或 Codex 努力实现的一个明确结果，例如修复错误、创建文档或研究某个主题。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页、移动端、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/app-server#threads\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">线程（Thread）（需联网）</a> — Codex 应用服务器 API 中的一种技术对象，其中包含对话轮次和已保存的会话历史记录。</li> <li>适用于: 应用服务器、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\">对话内定时任务（Scheduled task in a chat）</a> — 一种使用现有对话上下文，并把每次运行结果返回到该对话的定时任务。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/app-server#start-or-resume-a-thread\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">线程分叉（Thread fork）（需联网）</a> — 从现有线程的已保存历史记录分支出来的新线程。</li> <li>适用于: 应用服务器、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/app-server#core-primitives\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">轮次（Turn）（需联网）</a> — 对话中的一次交流，通常包括一条用户提示词，以及智能体的响应和操作。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展、云端、SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=web-search-mode\">网页搜索缓存（Web search cache）</a> — Codex 无需实时浏览即可使用的预先索引搜索结果。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669\">ChatGPT Work</a> — ChatGPT 中用于研究、分析，以及创建文档、演示文稿、电子表格和其它成品的智能体。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、网页</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">工作树（Worktree）</a> — Codex 在单独的 Git 工作树中隔离更改的模式。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=protected-paths-in-writable-roots\">可写根目录（Writable roots）</a> — 允许 Codex 修改的目录。</li> <li>适用于: 桌面应用、CLI、IDE 扩展</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"glossary\">Glossary</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use this glossary as a quick reference for Codex terms across the app, CLI, IDE extension, cloud, SDK, and related integrations.</p> <p><strong>Glossary</strong></p> <blockquote> <p>Search glossary terms; Filter by term, definition, or surface; No glossary terms match your search.</p> </blockquote> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\">Action</a> — An operation performed by a person, ChatGPT, or Codex, such as editing a file, running a command, or using a connected service.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web, Mobile, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Agent (online)</a> — The Codex agent that reasons over context, uses tools, and completes a task.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-94f17e3de1ca7cb3\">AGENTS.md</a> — Repository or user guidance file that gives Codex persistent instructions.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e8a44d8693c261b7\">Analytics dashboard</a> — Admin hub for ChatGPT workspace adoption and Codex-focused reporting.</li> <li>Applies to: Enterprise</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=sign-in-with-an-api-key\">API key sign-in</a> — Authentication using an OpenAI API key.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=sandbox-and-approvals\">Approval policy</a> — Rules for when Codex must ask before taking an action.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=automatic-approval-reviews\">Approval request</a> — Codex asking to allow a restricted action.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Apps (configuration)</a> — Codex configuration and app-server fields that store connector settings under the <code>apps</code> name.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302b8efa03eab38\">Appshot</a> — Snapshot of the frontmost app window sent to a ChatGPT or Codex chat.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=login-caching\">Auth cache</a> — Locally stored login credentials reused by Codex.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=automatic-approval-reviews\">Automatic approval review</a> — Model-based review of eligible approval requests before they proceed.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Scheduled task</a> — A prompt ChatGPT runs at a future time or on a recurring schedule, with its own settings and run history.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=managing-tasks\">Scheduled run</a> — One execution of a scheduled task, including its status and any resulting findings.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/browser?surface=app#app-computer-use-in-the-browser\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Computer Use in the browser (online)</a> — Capability that lets ChatGPT operate the built-in browser directly.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76?anchor=start-a-chat\">Chat</a> — A saved space for exchanging messages with ChatGPT or Codex, including shared context, results, and actions. Quick chat starts a ChatGPT chat from Codex.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web, Mobile, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115?anchor=sign-in-with-chatgpt\">ChatGPT sign-in</a> — Authentication using a ChatGPT account and workspace permissions.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f3a0216fc3d2956b\">Computer History</a> — Opt-in macOS feature that builds memories and a timeline from interaction events across allowed apps and websites.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex Cloud</a> — Coding tasks that run in the cloud with their own workspaces, repositories, and tools.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, IDE extension, Web</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1\">Cloud environment</a> — Reusable repositories, dependencies, tools, and access settings for tasks in Codex Cloud.</li> <li>Applies to: Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=how-codex-cloud-tasks-run\">Cloud chat</a> — A Codex chat that runs remotely in a cloud environment.</li> <li>Applies to: Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex (online)</a> — OpenAI's coding agent for software development tasks.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Web, Cloud, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT desktop app</a> — Desktop app with ChatGPT and Codex, including Chat and Work, projects, file previews, scheduled tasks, and developer tools.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex app-server</a> — Local JSON-RPC server for embedding Codex threads, turns, approvals, history, and streamed events in custom clients.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, IDE extension, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d\">Codex CLI</a> — Terminal client for running Codex interactively or in scripts.</li> <li>Applies to: Terminal</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">codex exec</a> — CLI command for running Codex non-interactively from scripts or CI.</li> <li>Applies to: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c7af5bbd57109077\">Codex IDE extension</a> — Editor integration for using Codex inside IDEs like VS Code, JetBrains IDEs, Cursor, and Windsurf.</li> <li>Applies to: IDE</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e3c5173f4c4c14ef\">Codex SDK</a> — Programmatic interface for building Codex-powered workflows or integrations.</li> <li>Applies to: SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=codex-managed-and-permanent-worktrees\">Codex-managed worktree</a> — A temporary worktree Codex creates and manages for a chat.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=context\">Compaction</a> — Summarizing older context so long-running work can continue.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-9d54fab7ad7294d0\">Compliance API</a> — API for exporting supported ChatGPT workspace records and audit metadata.</li> <li>Applies to: Enterprise</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7be3f970bd43699c\">Computer Use</a> — Desktop capability that lets ChatGPT interact with other applications through the UI.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713?anchor=configtoml\">config.toml</a> — Local Codex configuration files.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f?anchor=what-comes-from-the-connected-host\">Connected host</a> — Computer or development environment that provides files, tools, and shell access for ChatGPT or Codex chats opened through remote connections.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Mobile</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Connector</a> — A component of a plugin that connects ChatGPT or Codex to data and actions in an external service.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app (ChatGPT Work, Codex), Web (ChatGPT Work)</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76?anchor=start-a-chat\">Conversation</a> — The ongoing exchange of messages and shared context between a person and ChatGPT or Codex within a chat.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web, Mobile, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64?anchor=context\">Context</a> — Information Codex can use while working, such as files, prior messages, tool output, and instructions.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/api/docs/guides/conversation-state#managing-the-context-window\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Context window (online)</a> — The maximum amount of information the model can consider at once.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b?anchor=custom-agents\">Custom agent</a> — User-defined agent role with its own instructions and settings.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-4d7a5dc78b3c591e?anchor=deny-reads-with-exact-paths-or-globs\">Deny-read rule</a> — Filesystem permission rule that prevents Codex from reading sensitive paths or glob matches.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Enterprise</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/code-review?surface=app#app-what-changes-it-shows\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Diff (online)</a> — Set of Git file changes shown for inspection, comments, staging, or reverting.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Git, Review</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">Domain allowlist</a> — Set of domains allowed by a Codex Cloud environment’s network policy.</li> <li>Applies to: Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a\">Environment (local)</a> — Desktop app configuration that tells Codex how to set up worktrees for a project.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Worktree</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=environment-variables-and-secrets\">Environment variable</a> — Runtime configuration value available during task execution.</li> <li>Applies to: Cloud, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a?anchor=basic-usage\">Ephemeral session</a> — Non-interactive run that skips saving session state after it completes.</li> <li>Applies to: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-55cdea3737e39583?anchor=fast-mode\">Fast mode</a> — Speed setting that makes supported models respond faster at a higher credit cost.</li> <li>Applies to: CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-4d7a5dc78b3c591e?anchor=filesystem-permissions\">Filesystem permission</a> — Permission profile rule that grants or denies read and write access to paths.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=managing-tasks\">Finding</a> — A notable result or issue surfaced by a scheduled task.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004?anchor=configure-defaults\">Full access</a> — Mode where Codex runs without normal sandbox restrictions.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=whats-a-worktree\">Git worktree</a> — A second checkout of the same repository for parallel branch work.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Git</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=working-between-local-and-worktree\">Handoff</a> — Moving a chat and its work between Local and Worktree.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\">Heartbeat</a> — A recurring scheduled task that returns ChatGPT to the same chat.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4\">Hook</a> — A lifecycle handler that runs when a Codex event matches, such as tool use, permission requests, or when a turn stops.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0aecdb1ef0cec0a4?anchor=config-shape\">Hook event</a> — Lifecycle point where configured hook handlers can run.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/code-review?surface=app#app-staging-and-reverting-files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hunk (online)</a> — Contiguous section of a diff that can be staged, unstaged, or reverted independently.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Git, Review</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/code-review?surface=app#app-inline-comments-for-feedback\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Inline comment (online)</a> — Line-specific feedback attached to a diff.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=web-search-mode\">Live web search</a> — Real-time web lookup for current information.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=working-between-local-and-worktree\">Local</a> — Mode where Codex works on the user's computer.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-275a09b4f8630225\">Local chat</a> — A ChatGPT or Codex chat that runs on the user's machine.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e\">Managed configuration</a> — Organization-controlled Codex defaults and restrictions.</li> <li>Applies to: Enterprise</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">MCP</a> — Model Context Protocol, a standard for connecting Codex to external tools and context.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=supported-mcp-features\">MCP resource</a> — Readable context exposed by an MCP server for Codex to inspect.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=supported-mcp-features\">MCP server</a> — External tool or context provider exposed through MCP.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=supported-mcp-features\">MCP tool</a> — Action exposed by an MCP server that Codex can call during a task.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-77481efb12a63f4e?anchor=macos-managed-preferences-mdm\">MDM</a> — Mobile device management tooling for distributing device profiles and managed Codex settings.</li> <li>Applies to: Enterprise</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ea5a1f5cc6a25bc\">Memories</a> — Locally stored context Codex can reuse across sessions.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">Model</a> — The AI model Codex uses for reasoning and tool work.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=network-access\">Network access</a> — Permission for commands or environments to reach the internet.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=network-policy\">Network policy</a> — Domain-based allow and deny rules that constrain sandboxed outbound network traffic.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">Non-interactive mode</a> — CLI mode for running Codex from scripts or CI.</li> <li>Applies to: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a?anchor=create-structured-outputs-with-a-schema\">Output schema</a> — JSON Schema passed to <code>codex exec</code> to constrain the final response.</li> <li>Applies to: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306?anchor=codex-managed-and-permanent-worktrees\">Permanent worktree</a> — A long-lived worktree kept as its own project.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-4d7a5dc78b3c591e?anchor=define-and-select-a-profile\">Permission profile</a> — Named least-privilege policy that combines filesystem and network rules for local command execution.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3e83237203418633?anchor=plan-first-for-difficult-tasks\">Plan</a> — Codex's proposed or tracked steps for completing a task.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugin</a> — An installable bundle of capabilities, such as skills, connectors, and tools, distributed through the universal directory shared by ChatGPT and Codex.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app (ChatGPT Work, Codex), Web (ChatGPT Work), CLI</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/plugins/build/plugins.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Plugin manifest</a> — Plugin metadata file that identifies a plugin and points to bundled skills, connector mappings, MCP servers, hooks, and metadata.</li> <li>Applies to: Plugin authoring</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6c7aa55b479f9cdd?anchor=understand-the-rules-language\">Prefix rule</a> — Command-rule pattern that allows, prompts for, or forbids matching command prefixes.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Enterprise</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b011aa51b3319b85?anchor=profiles\">Profile</a> — Named configuration preset for Codex.</li> <li>Applies to: CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Progressive disclosure</a> — Loading skill details only when needed to preserve context.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web (ChatGPT Work), CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">Project</a> — A group of related chats and shared sources, or a local folder used for file-based work.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0310706ee8617b64\">Prompt</a> — A question, instruction, or goal sent to ChatGPT or Codex.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/code-review?surface=app#app-pull-request-reviews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pull request review (online)</a> — Codex review of changes or feedback on a pull request.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, GitHub</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8\">RBAC</a> — Role-based access control for workspace permissions.</li> <li>Applies to: Enterprise</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">Read-only mode</a> — Mode where Codex can inspect but not modify without approval.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=reasoning-effort\">Reasoning effort</a> — Setting that controls how much reasoning budget a model uses.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-171fdaa74f75310f\">Remote connection</a> — Connection that lets you access ChatGPT or Codex chats on another device through a connected host.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Mobile</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713?anchor=requirementstoml\">requirements.toml</a> — Admin-enforced requirements file for managed Codex setups.</li> <li>Applies to: Enterprise</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">Review pane</a> — Desktop app view for inspecting diffs, comments, and Git changes.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-6c7aa55b479f9cdd\">Rules</a> — Policies that allow, prompt for, or deny command prefixes or permission exceptions.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-668fd22585595004\">Sandbox</a> — Enforced boundary limiting what Codex commands can access or modify.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=sandbox-level\">Sandbox mode</a> — Configuration that defines Codex's filesystem and network limits.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-e3c5173f4c4c14ef?anchor=sandbox-presets\">Sandbox preset</a> — SDK shorthand for common sandbox policies such as read-only, workspace-write, or full access.</li> <li>Applies to: SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Schedule</a> — The timing rule for a scheduled task.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=environment-variables-and-secrets\">Network secret</a> — A credential for a specific HTTPS service. Programs receive a placeholder; the proxy substitutes the credential for allowed destinations during setup and tasks.</li> <li>Applies to: Codex Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-86cde8be2e24d05a?anchor=setup-scripts\">Setup script</a> — Script run before the agent starts to install dependencies or prepare tools.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app worktrees</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Skill</a> — Reusable workflow package with instructions and optional scripts or references.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web (ChatGPT Work), CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23?anchor=how-codex-uses-skills\">Skill invocation</a> — Explicit or implicit activation of a skill.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web (ChatGPT Work), CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Slash command</a> — Command entered with a leading slash to control or inspect a Codex CLI session.</li> <li>Applies to: CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68\">Standalone scheduled task</a> — Scheduled task whose runs each start a new chat and report findings in Triage.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=stdio-servers\">STDIO MCP server</a> — MCP server launched as a local process by a configured command and arguments.</li> <li>Applies to: CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb?anchor=streamable-http-servers\">Streamable HTTP MCP server</a> — MCP server reached over HTTP, optionally with bearer token or OAuth authentication.</li> <li>Applies to: CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\">Subagent</a> — Specialized child agent spawned to work on part of a task.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b?anchor=core-terms\">Subagent workflow</a> — Workflow where Codex runs delegated agents in parallel and combines their results.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">Standalone task</a> — A Codex task that isn't grouped within a project.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-3353f8f8f4d90d76\">Task</a> — A defined outcome ChatGPT or Codex works toward, such as fixing a bug, creating a document, or researching a topic.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web, Mobile, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/app-server#threads\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Thread (online)</a> — A technical object in Codex app-server APIs that contains turns and stored conversation history.</li> <li>Applies to: App-server, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b5406e60cbfa0b68?anchor=schedule-a-task-inside-a-chat\">Scheduled task in a chat</a> — A scheduled task that uses an existing chat's context and returns each run's results to that chat.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/app-server#start-or-resume-a-thread\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Thread fork (online)</a> — New thread branched from the stored history of an existing thread.</li> <li>Applies to: App-server, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/app-server#core-primitives\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Turn (online)</a> — One exchange in a chat, usually a user prompt plus the agent's response and actions.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension, Cloud, SDK</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=web-search-mode\">Web search cache</a> — Pre-indexed search results Codex can use without live browsing.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2c7688c996bc9669\">ChatGPT Work</a> — The agent in ChatGPT for research, analysis, and creating documents, presentations, spreadsheets, and other finished work.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, Web</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d955137d94c4d306\">Worktree</a> — Mode where Codex isolates changes in a separate Git worktree.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3?anchor=protected-paths-in-writable-roots\">Writable roots</a> — Directories Codex is allowed to modify.</li> <li>Applies to: Desktop app, CLI, IDE extension</li> </ul>"};
